# Always Push Code

After completing any code changes in this project:

1. Commit the changes with a clear message (unless the user said not to commit).
2. Immediately `git push` to `origin` on the current branch (usually `main`).
3. Do this by default without waiting for the user to ask — the user wants code pushed every time.

If push needs approval or fails, retry/fix and tell the user the result with the repo URL.
